hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20614","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Kahmas narrated to us, and Yazid said: Kahmas informed us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq say: Mihjan ibn al-Adra' said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on an errand, then he met me while I was coming out from one of the roads of Madinah. He said: So I went with him until we climbed Uhud. He turned toward Madinah and said: Woe to it as a town, on the day its people will abandon it, Yazid said: at its ripest as it can be. He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, who will eat its fruit? He said: The healthy ones of birds and beasts. He said: And the Dajjal will not enter it; whenever he intends to enter it he is met at every mountain pass of it by an angel with drawn sword. He said: Then we came down until when we were at the door of the mosque, he said: There was a man praying. He said: Do you say that truthfully? He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, this is so-and-so, and he is among the best of the people of Madinah, or he said: the most praying of the people of Madinah. He said: Do not let him hear, lest you destroy him, two times or three times. You are an ummah for whom ease is intended."
"20615","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to me, from Abu Bishr, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq narrate from Raja' ibn Abi Raja' al-Bahili, from Mihjan, a man of Aslam, and he mentioned the like of it."
"20616","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Raja' ibn Abi Raja' al-Bahili, from Mihjan, Affan said: and he is Ibn al-Adra'."
"20617","And Hammad narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Mihjan ibn al-Adra', he said: Raja' said: I came with Mihjan one day until when we reached the mosque of Basrah we found Buraydah al-Aslami sitting at one of the doors of the mosque. He said: And in the mosque there was a man called Sukbah who prolonged the prayer. When we reached the door of the mosque where Buraydah was, he said: And Buraydah was a man given to jesting. He said: O Mihjan, will you not pray as Sukbah prays? He said: Mihjan did not answer him anything and went back. He said: And Mihjan said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and went walking until he climbed Uhud and looked over Madinah. He said: Woe to it as a town, which its people will leave at its most flourishing as it can be. The Dajjal will come to it and find at every gate of its gates an angel with drawn sword, so he will not enter it. He said: Then he descended until when we were at the threshold of the mosque, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying in the mosque, bowing and prostrating and bowing and prostrating. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Who is this? He said: So I began to praise him to him. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is so-and-so and this and this. He said: Be silent, do not let him hear, lest you destroy him. He said: Then he went walking until when we were at a chamber, but he let go of my hand, then he said: The best of your religion is its easiest, the best of your religion is its easiest, the best of your religion is its easiest."
